Let's go.

277
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:15,200
I need to give that cat a fish ASAP.

278
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:20,320
Oh, you know what I want to do here?

279
00:24:21,220 --> 00:24:23,180
I want to make, like, a roof.

280
00:24:25,990 --> 00:24:26,990
In case it's raining.

281
00:24:32,530 --> 00:24:33,770
Look how good this is.

282
00:24:33,930 --> 00:24:35,070
Immediately got a fish.

283
00:24:40,420 --> 00:24:42,320
I wonder if there's a higher luck of the sea.

284
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:47,780
Oh, and I'm getting experience from this.

285
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:49,160
It's actually huge.

286
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:53,320
I should be doing more fishing in general.

287
00:24:54,180 --> 00:24:56,200
Because I get experience, I get fish.

288
00:24:56,300 --> 00:24:57,540
It's good food too, you know.

289
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:58,760
Fish are pretty good.

290
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:01,440
And there's a chance to getting something crazy.

291
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:08,940
The craziest thing I've gotten is another fishing rod that was really good.

292
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:11,520
Even better than the fishing rod I was using to fish up the fishing rod.

293
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:14,300
That was better than my fishing rod.

294
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,620
Not the better one, but the worst fishing rod.

295
00:25:17,060 --> 00:25:17,820
You know what I mean.

296
00:25:31,420 --> 00:25:32,800
That's kind of disturbing, isn't it?

297
00:25:34,860 --> 00:25:37,060
I... I don't like that, actually.

298
00:25:38,600 --> 00:25:39,440
I need to kill you.

299
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:39,840
I'm sorry.

300
00:25:40,960 --> 00:25:45,680
I'm sorry for... What?

301
00:25:47,020 --> 00:25:49,560
He pooped himself to death right after I hit him.

302
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:50,480
I didn't kill him.

303
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:53,420
I don't understand what just happened.

304
00:25:54,020 --> 00:25:54,780
That was weird.

305
00:25:55,740 --> 00:25:57,480
In fact, the way he was pooping...

306
00:25:58,410 --> 00:26:01,770
According to Newton's laws, that boat should be going off, you know?

307
00:26:02,090 --> 00:26:02,790
But it wasn't.

308
00:26:03,870 --> 00:26:05,110
It's like a rocket engine.

309
00:26:07,750 --> 00:26:09,750
Physics are indeed not true in this game.

310
00:26:10,430 --> 00:26:12,310
Nautilus shell, that is used for something.

311
00:26:16,430 --> 00:26:18,350
And whatever it's used for, I need a lot of it.

312
00:26:18,550 --> 00:26:19,310
I remember that much.

313
00:26:28,140 --> 00:26:29,840
I think it needed raw fish.

314
00:26:32,540 --> 00:26:34,220
The cat.

315
00:26:35,540 --> 00:26:36,480
Okay, that should be enough.

316
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:40,940
Actually, it may not be enough.

317
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:43,940
Sometimes they eat them and they don't become your friend.

318
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:45,260
Just like the bones, right?

319
00:26:45,820 --> 00:26:46,620
On the dogs.

320
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:53,560
Huh, I thought I released that cow.

321
00:26:58,410 --> 00:26:58,810
Weird.

322
00:26:58,810 --> 00:27:01,870
Now, there is actually something going on up on that roof as well.

323
00:27:03,730 --> 00:27:04,730
What did I do here?

324
00:27:04,810 --> 00:27:06,390
What did I put down that is not good?

325
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:12,980
Remember how the villagers used to go on top of the roof?

326
00:27:13,100 --> 00:27:14,820
I think there's something going on down here as well.

327
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:17,020
Maybe it was the blast furnace that I had there.

328
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:19,700
But why wouldn't they just go in through the door, right?

329
00:27:22,220 --> 00:27:24,120
There's definitely something about that spot.

330
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:25,200
They love that spot.

331
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:27,600
Kitty cat?

332
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:30,660
Oh, you know what?

333
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:32,020
I think the kitty cat appeared.

334
00:27:33,380 --> 00:27:35,340
Because I have enough villagers, maybe.

335
00:27:35,770 --> 00:27:38,470
You know how villagers out in the wild always have cats?

336
00:27:38,630 --> 00:27:39,590
Or at least a lot of them do.

337
00:27:41,010 --> 00:27:43,470
Maybe cats just spawn when you have enough villagers.

338
00:27:45,530 --> 00:27:46,190
You know what I mean?

339
00:27:47,110 --> 00:27:48,170
It's gotta be like that.

340
00:27:50,330 --> 00:27:50,990
Where's the cat?

341
00:27:56,410 --> 00:27:57,610
I'm trying to listen for it.

342
00:28:05,180 --> 00:28:05,700
Flame.

343
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:10,480
Um... Actually, yes.

344
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:13,160
Wait a minute, flame?

345
00:28:13,660 --> 00:28:14,960
Flame, flame, flame.

346
00:28:15,540 --> 00:28:18,080
That is on the bow, isn't it?

347
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:20,860
The sword was fire aspect.

348
00:28:21,140 --> 00:28:22,080
Or maybe it was the other way around.

349
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:27,480
Well, I don't have one right now, fuck.

350
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:29,560
I think it's on the bow.

351
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:34,140
I definitely need one of those so that I can cook food in the wild.

352
00:28:35,020 --> 00:28:36,580
I think I'm gonna buy this off of him.

353
00:28:37,380 --> 00:28:38,920
Oh, here's what I'm gonna do today.

354
00:28:39,340 --> 00:28:42,840
I will actually try to level up villagers and earn money.

355
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:44,780
I'm gonna be doing a lot of trading today.

356
00:28:45,540 --> 00:28:48,940
Because I want a lot of emeralds, otherwise I can't even get mending, right?

357
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:51,900
I need to do that.

358
00:28:53,270 --> 00:28:54,430
Let's get rid of this chest.

359
00:28:55,870 --> 00:28:57,470
Maybe we can have more beds in here.

360
00:28:58,730 --> 00:28:59,310
Or something.

361
00:28:59,450 --> 00:29:01,030
I don't even know what this place is supposed to be.

362
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:03,870
Honestly, it looks a little bit like a church.

363
00:29:04,470 --> 00:29:05,190
Then again, not really.

364
00:29:07,750 --> 00:29:08,110
Flame.

365
00:29:08,810 --> 00:29:10,590
How much emerald do I have?

366
00:29:11,330 --> 00:29:13,050
If I have 14, I may actually buy it.

367
00:29:13,170 --> 00:29:13,990
Shit, I have two.

368
00:29:15,130 --> 00:29:15,730
That's it?

369
00:29:19,850 --> 00:29:20,470
Kitty cat!

370
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:24,760
Where are you?

371
00:29:27,020 --> 00:29:28,180
Did I leave a door open?

372
00:29:28,340 --> 00:29:28,440
No.

373
00:29:29,540 --> 00:29:29,900
Okay, wait.

374
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:30,800
Are you making your way out?

375
00:29:34,040 --> 00:29:35,580
Nope, you cannot get out.

376
00:29:37,580 --> 00:29:38,020
Fletcher.

377
00:29:40,260 --> 00:29:44,560
Where the fuck are you working out from?

378
00:29:47,020 --> 00:29:47,920
Where's your office?

379
00:29:49,420 --> 00:29:51,100
That was the whole mystery last time.

380
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:52,080
ODB!

381
00:29:52,940 --> 00:29:54,260
He likes to hang out behind the house.

382
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:56,100
Would you like a fish?

383
00:29:57,260 --> 00:29:58,900
Maybe it's the shield that's fucking this up.

384
00:29:59,040 --> 00:30:00,260
Oh, my shield is almost gone, by the way.

385
00:30:01,100 --> 00:30:02,600
In that case, I'm just gonna throw it.

386
00:30:03,220 --> 00:30:03,720
Fuck it.

387
00:30:06,560 --> 00:30:07,340
You're not Ginny.

388
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,420
Throw it here.

389
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:15,320
Nice!

390
00:30:16,020 --> 00:30:16,680
Good job.

391
00:30:18,020 --> 00:30:19,280
And... what was I doing?

392
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:21,500
Oh yeah.

393
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:23,320
You like fish, ODB?

394
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:24,960
You don't.

395
00:30:24,980 --> 00:30:25,940
What about some berries?

396
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:26,460
No?

397
00:30:27,580 --> 00:30:27,980
Taters?

398
00:30:28,320 --> 00:30:28,640
Nope.

399
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:32,060
You don't like ink, right?

400
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,040
By the way, I feel like I would have hurt the cat by now.

401
00:30:38,260 --> 00:30:40,220
Wait a minute, cats can climb things, right?

402
00:30:41,620 --> 00:30:43,540
Maybe the cat climbed out of here somehow.

403
00:30:43,760 --> 00:30:44,880
I don't know how cats operate.

404
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:51,020
I mean, in real life, they climb everywhere, right?

405
00:30:51,200 --> 00:30:53,020
So you can't really contain them like this.

406
00:30:53,260 --> 00:30:53,820
No way.

407
00:30:55,280 --> 00:30:57,740
So it's probably gone, to be honest.

408
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,500
I'll try and pay attention next time.

409
00:31:02,780 --> 00:31:03,780
When it's close by.

410
00:31:04,220 --> 00:31:05,380
I'm gonna have the fish ready.

411
00:31:05,820 --> 00:31:06,900
Let's put them in a bundle.

412
00:31:08,140 --> 00:31:08,740
This one.

413
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:11,900
Now we have fish ready.

414
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:14,840
This one does unfortunately not fit in one of those.

415
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:16,260
Nautilus Shell.

416
00:31:16,380 --> 00:31:17,420
Do I have any right now?

417
00:31:20,760 --> 00:31:21,660
Here's a trick I can do.

418
00:31:22,260 --> 00:31:22,660
Double click.

419
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:24,520
If nothing happens, it means there's nothing up here.

420
00:31:26,740 --> 00:31:27,100
Drops.

421
00:31:27,780 --> 00:31:28,140
Nothing.

422
00:31:29,060 --> 00:31:30,200
That's actually a genius trick.

423
00:31:30,560 --> 00:31:31,940
Holy shit, I should have used that earlier.

424
00:31:32,780 --> 00:31:33,940
But I think this is all I have.

425
00:31:35,380 --> 00:31:35,740
Miscellaneous.

426
00:31:37,540 --> 00:31:38,120
Some berries.

427
00:31:38,220 --> 00:31:40,780
I wonder if I can make some kind of berry pie.

428
00:31:42,340 --> 00:31:43,040
Or something.

429
00:31:43,180 --> 00:31:43,840
Can I make pie?

430
00:31:44,120 --> 00:31:44,440
Hey!

431
00:31:45,500 --> 00:31:46,220
Pumpkin pie, though.

432
00:31:48,420 --> 00:31:49,620
Egg, sugar, and pumpkin.

433
00:31:51,420 --> 00:31:52,820
Yo, I wonder how good that is.

434
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:56,220
Pumpkin is actually... I have a lot of that!

435
00:31:56,760 --> 00:31:58,600
I'm gonna keep one, though, in case I need to farm it.

436
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:05,740
Sugar is from sugar cane, which is... here.

437
00:32:07,060 --> 00:32:08,160
I must have more, no?

438
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:13,680
Twenty... And what was the last one?

439
00:32:14,980 --> 00:32:15,660
Pie?

440
00:32:17,420 --> 00:32:18,100
Eggs.

441
00:32:20,260 --> 00:32:21,120
That's it!

442
00:32:22,900 --> 00:32:24,040
Okay, thank god.

443
00:32:29,220 --> 00:32:30,520
Thirteen pumpkin pies.

444
00:32:31,620 --> 00:32:32,740
Now we're cooking.

445
00:32:34,940 --> 00:32:36,560
Sugar back, potato back.

446
00:32:40,330 --> 00:32:41,310
I'm gonna store it here.

447
00:32:41,510 --> 00:32:43,910
I do want to eat my baked potatoes while I'm at home.

448
00:32:45,070 --> 00:32:45,730
Armor stand.

449
00:32:48,450 --> 00:32:49,510
We can put this somewhere.

450
00:32:49,770 --> 00:32:50,830
Maybe upstairs, actually.

451
00:32:52,190 --> 00:32:53,890
We need some more furniture up here, right?

452
00:32:55,910 --> 00:32:56,950
This can be right here.

453
00:33:00,070 --> 00:33:01,410
Sure, let's put some gold on it.

454
00:33:06,430 --> 00:33:07,230
There we go.

455
00:33:07,830 --> 00:33:08,730
Look at that.

456
00:33:09,630 --> 00:33:10,150
Wonderful.

457
00:33:11,890 --> 00:33:12,410
Channeling.

458
00:33:13,230 --> 00:33:14,290
Oh, that's right.

459
00:33:14,470 --> 00:33:17,350
I needed to remove more barrels over here.

460
00:33:17,710 --> 00:33:19,250
There's barrels inside of here.

461
00:33:20,010 --> 00:33:20,830
Barrels are bad.

462
00:33:21,030 --> 00:33:21,530
We learned that.

463
00:33:23,250 --> 00:33:24,090
Oh, god.

464
00:33:24,610 --> 00:33:24,970
Okay.

465
00:33:25,170 --> 00:33:26,170
What is a good way to do this?

466
00:33:26,950 --> 00:33:28,230
Using chests, of course.

467
00:33:29,210 --> 00:33:32,470
I mean, all this is actually temporary anyway.

468
00:33:34,720 --> 00:33:35,560
So it's fine.

469
00:33:36,300 --> 00:33:37,180
Put that in there.

470
00:33:39,300 --> 00:33:40,360
Let's just do this for now.

471
00:33:40,760 --> 00:33:40,920
Shit.

472
00:33:45,190 --> 00:33:46,770
Yeah, just do this.

473
00:33:48,150 --> 00:33:48,930
It's fine.

474
00:33:50,150 --> 00:33:51,150
Click it all inside.

475
00:33:52,330 --> 00:33:54,250
We also have stuff up in another barrel.

476
00:33:54,410 --> 00:33:55,190
I think I destroyed that then.

477
00:33:57,990 --> 00:33:58,930
Cannot have barrels.

478
00:33:59,570 --> 00:34:00,350
It's not allowed.

479
00:34:02,630 --> 00:34:04,830
Barrels make... fishermen.

480
00:34:05,670 --> 00:34:07,730
Oh, I should have a barrel on the pier then!

481
00:34:07,970 --> 00:34:09,850
But then again, I don't want villagers out there.

482
00:34:10,290 --> 00:34:11,890
So never mind, actually.

483
00:34:12,970 --> 00:34:26,070
I do wonder... if I put a barrel on the pier... or the dock... if they're gonna go out there and fish... and then put fish in the barrel... essentially creating free food for me.

484
00:34:26,970 --> 00:34:28,210
That would be insane.

485
00:34:29,270 --> 00:34:30,630
Imagine if that's what's going on.

486
00:34:32,230 --> 00:34:33,110
I would love that.

487
00:34:37,010 --> 00:34:37,950
In you go.

488
00:34:38,130 --> 00:34:38,450
Perfect.

489
00:34:39,130 --> 00:34:40,090
Lapis lazuli.

490
00:34:40,630 --> 00:34:42,710
I'm gonna turn this into this...

491
00:34:45,610 --> 00:34:48,450
It's just easier, you know, when I actually have to enchant.

492
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:51,830
I kind of like the chest on top of the bookshelves, actually.

493
00:34:52,530 --> 00:34:53,910
This also looks way better.

494
00:34:55,290 --> 00:34:56,330
Really happy with that.

495
00:34:58,010 --> 00:35:01,010
And the chiseled ones I am very unhappy with, actually.

496
00:35:01,130 --> 00:35:02,830
I would like to use normal bookshelves here.

497
00:35:02,950 --> 00:35:06,330
But this place is temporary, so let's just not go crazy right now.

498
00:35:06,910 --> 00:35:08,390
Put something like that there for now.

499
00:35:09,870 --> 00:35:10,250
Yeah.

500
00:35:10,870 --> 00:35:13,290
Okay, another potential issue fixed with the village.

501
00:35:14,730 --> 00:35:15,530
So satisfying.

502
00:35:17,030 --> 00:35:17,850
I gotta be careful.

503
00:35:18,030 --> 00:35:19,350
I can't put blast furnaces anywhere.

504
00:35:19,470 --> 00:35:22,030
This is actually a problem with living in a village now, I realize.

505
00:35:24,150 --> 00:35:27,070
Unless I want one of them to be a blast furnace person.

506
00:35:29,050 --> 00:35:30,150
Blast furnace person.

507
00:35:31,270 --> 00:35:33,090
Then I just have to go there and use it.

508
00:35:33,290 --> 00:35:33,970
I don't mind.

509
00:35:34,510 --> 00:35:35,810
But right now I need mending.

510
00:35:35,950 --> 00:35:37,090
That's like the number one thing.

511
00:35:37,530 --> 00:35:38,470
So let's go to bed.

512
00:35:38,950 --> 00:35:39,390
You know what?

513
00:35:39,410 --> 00:35:40,010
We need more beds.

514
00:35:40,570 --> 00:35:41,170
Fucking hell.

515
00:35:43,070 --> 00:35:44,190
Can I use mine up here?

516
00:35:45,890 --> 00:35:47,430
Okay, that one is not occupied.

517
00:35:47,750 --> 00:35:48,410
Thank God.

518
00:35:49,570 --> 00:35:53,010
But I am going to need more beds anyway, because... we need more villagers.

519
00:35:55,230 --> 00:35:57,710
It's not quite the bustling village I had in mind.

520
00:35:58,170 --> 00:35:58,830
Just yet.

521
00:36:01,110 --> 00:36:02,630
Oh, I definitely have wool, though.

522
00:36:05,070 --> 00:36:06,410
I have mucho wool.

523
00:36:07,310 --> 00:36:08,990
And we need wood, I believe.

524
00:36:09,730 --> 00:36:10,270
That's it.

525
00:36:13,160 --> 00:36:15,180
Bunch of... white beds are so boring.

526
00:36:15,900 --> 00:36:16,720
Here's what we're gonna do.

527
00:36:16,860 --> 00:36:18,860
We're gonna have a separate color for each profession.

528
00:36:26,860 --> 00:36:27,960
How do I color them?

529
00:36:33,490 --> 00:36:33,890
Oh!

530
00:36:33,890 --> 00:36:34,290
Fuck.

531
00:36:35,130 --> 00:36:37,530
I need to color the wool before I make the bed.

532
00:36:37,690 --> 00:36:39,390
I can't color the bed after it's been made.

533
00:36:40,310 --> 00:36:40,710
Shit!

534
00:36:42,990 --> 00:36:44,350
God damn it.

535
00:36:44,490 --> 00:36:44,950
Okay, you know what?

536
00:36:44,970 --> 00:36:47,330
We have some beds for future exploration purposes.

537
00:36:48,970 --> 00:36:49,570
That's fine.

538
00:36:50,410 --> 00:36:50,810
Wool.

539
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:51,590
Wool, wool, wool.

540
00:36:54,470 --> 00:36:55,510
Blue, wool, white.

541
00:36:55,810 --> 00:36:56,930
Can I really not make more?

542
00:36:57,650 --> 00:36:58,390
Oh, I can.

543
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:05,210
Pink, grey, red dye, nice.

544
00:37:05,950 --> 00:37:08,410
I definitely need a dye chest.

545
00:37:11,930 --> 00:37:12,930
Light gray wool?

546
00:37:13,070 --> 00:37:13,610
I have that already.

547
00:37:13,930 --> 00:37:15,290
But I need three, I believe.

548
00:37:16,930 --> 00:37:18,350
Oh shit, then this won't be enough.

549
00:37:18,530 --> 00:37:19,010
Oh no!

550
00:37:21,290 --> 00:37:23,430
I need to get colors going, man!

551
00:37:23,590 --> 00:37:24,270
